cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, or the derived catalogs it produces, please cite it
  using the metadata below. If you use the derived catalog, please also cite the
  Japan Meteorological Agency Seismological Bulletin as its source and state
  that the files here are edited derivatives, as set out in the NOTICE file.
title: >-
  Project Sentinel Block 1: region, target catalog and magnitude completeness
  for a pre-registered forecast evaluation on the CSEP-Japan All Japan region
abstract: >-
  This release contains the foundation of a pre-registered earthquake forecast
  evaluation and none of the evaluation itself. No forecast has been produced
  and no result exists. Block 1 establishes the region geometry, the evaluation
  window, the magnitude threshold with its secondary analysis and negative
  control, a target catalog of 4,442 events built from 2,161,892 raw JMA
  Seismological Bulletin records under nine pre-registered selection rules, and
  magnitude completeness estimated under a protocol locked before any estimate
  existed. Every locked decision is recorded in an append-only registration
  ledger carrying a SHA-256 of each file.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-24'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/synexisproject-bit/project-sentinel'
